<section image-layout="blank" id="XFfpx8WVRO" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="A_WZvm7Qdt" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">A true story from southern Brazil</p><h1 font-size="48pt">The War of the Rags</h1><p font-size="lg">How cattle, salt, taxes and an astonishing boat journey shaped a ten-year revolt.</p><spacer size="24pt"></spacer><hr color="palette-3" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="sm">The Ragamuffin War · 1835–1845</p></grid-item><grid-item id="X8GtIKF4uN" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/zZwpOJp6OYcuYhn90_bt1.png" saved-media-id="kmopo5n9db39lbf" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper museum-table illustration on warm cream paper, a folded map of southern Brazil beside a strip of salted dried beef, a wooden salt scoop, old coins and a travel bag, postcard red, river blue and sun yellow accents, soft colored-pencil shading, visible paper edges, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ee4eysCuqf"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="lPVe3k3PSw"><h2>Brazil's cattle corner</h2><p>Rio Grande do Sul sits at Brazil's very bottom, beside Uruguay and Argentina.</p><freeform-block w="844" h="300"><box type="content" w="844" h="300" sizing="fixed"><custom-code>
            <style>
              .rag-map { width: 844px; height: 300px; font-family: var(--body-font); }
              .rag-map .country { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-color) 72%, white); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 3; stroke-linejoin: round; }
              .rag-map .south { fill: var(--accent-color); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 3; }
              .rag-map .sea { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--palette-2) 18%, transparent); }
              .rag-map .route { fill: none; stroke: var(--palette-2); stroke-width: 4; stroke-dasharray: 10 8; }
              .rag-map .pin { fill: var(--palette-3); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 3; }
            </style>
            <svg class="rag-map" width="844" height="300" viewBox="0 0 844 300" role="img" aria-label="Schematic map of Brazil showing Rio Grande do Sul in the far south and Rio de Janeiro far to the north">
              <rect class="sea" x="0" y="0" width="844" height="300" rx="20"></rect>
              <path class="country" d="M318 18 L393 31 L443 60 L486 73 L515 110 L493 139 L508 172 L477 198 L461 239 L424 281 L376 267 L354 232 L319 211 L305 174 L278 151 L290 111 L270 81 L298 57 Z"></path>
              <path class="south" d="M376 267 L424 281 L461 239 L427 230 L397 243 Z"></path>
              <path class="route" d="M421 252 C516 220 555 156 577 96"></path>
              <circle class="pin" cx="577" cy="96" r="10"></circle>
              <circle class="pin" cx="420" cy="252" r="10"></circle>
            </svg>
          </custom-code></box><shape preset="line" x="579" y="88" w="80" h="2" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="420" y="252" w="112" h="2" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><box type="content" x="651" y="50" w="175" h="82" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 12pt 14pt; border-radius: 10pt;"><h4>Rio de Janeiro</h4><p font-size="sm">The capital, about 2,000 km away. The journey took weeks by horse.</p></box><box type="content" x="508" y="214" w="230" h="70" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 11pt 14pt; border-radius: 10pt;"><h4>Rio Grande do Sul</h4><p font-size="sm">Grassy plains, huge cattle herds and gaúcho cowboys.</p></box></freeform-block><p role="caption">Schematic map · <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Source: Ragamuffin War overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="XVm-e9G1fE"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="2Axkana0hL" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/nR826MsrWpZ_38c9bsoe2.png" saved-media-id="h741yovjf1rdahf" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper still life on warm cream paper, one strip of salted dried beef, a wooden scoop spilling coarse salt and a small old coin, arranged like museum objects with postcard red, river blue and sun yellow labels without lettering, soft colored-pencil shadows, no people, no text" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="-xaXrnR9SW" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><h2>It started with beef jerky</h2><grid marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" spacing="small"><grid-item id="WltrULa0GK" cell-style="subtle"><h4>Charque kept for months</h4><p>Charque is beef dried with salt. It was the south's biggest product.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Bu_F9KuVxa" cell-style="subtle"><h4>Two heavy taxes</h4><p>The government taxed the charque and the salt needed to make it.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UHzN3Pahu0" cell-style="subtle"><h4>Cheaper rivals</h4><p>Charque from Uruguay and Argentina was barely taxed, so it cost less.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://brasilescola.uol.com.br/guerras/guerra-dos-farrapos.htm">Source: Brasil Escola</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="wvNmksGec9"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="mYSbCo6vZF" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><h2>Who was making the rules?</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" spacing="medium"><grid-item id="KU9BaiwkTS"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/zEBF0hcAUsSZdekev1DF.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="child emperor crown throne" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A minimalist icon of a child's silhouette with a rounded head and a simple body, conveying the concept of childhood or youth in a straightforward and recognizable visual form.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>A boy emperor</h4><p>Pedro II was nine. Grown-up regents ruled in his name.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="WMjEqFvL1E"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/TdMPyZspSPZT2sk727EX.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="stack of tax papers" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A document icon featuring a single sheet of paper with a folded corner.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>A distant capital</h4><p>Southern ranchers said Rio took their taxes and ignored local problems.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Q9I5MDpedV"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/RokLZJ3xQq5UYlrroC2C.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="map divided into provinces" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black shape of a crown, symbolizing the concept of a province, often associated with a regional or geographical area within a larger country, typically having its own administrative and governmental structures.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>More local say</h4><p>They wanted each province to decide more for itself.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Source: Encyclopedia.com</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="w77cn4jYGS" padding="0" colspan="25"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/zxUPNCY99s_k0DA3HK3SG.png" saved-media-id="dew2ssn2mup3j4i" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper illustration of a nine-year-old Brazilian emperor seated quietly on an oversized formal throne beside a towering stack of tax papers, dignified restrained expression, historically grounded general 1830s clothing, warm cream paper, postcard red, river blue and sun yellow accents, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="IlL3or0mKB" background-color="surface"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="rZI3H6eYgY" vertical-align="center" colspan="31"><p role="eyebrow">An insult becomes a badge</p><display size="lg">Farrapo</display><h3 role="subheading">means “rag” in Portuguese.</h3><p>Enemies mocked the rebels' fringed leather clothes. The rebels kept the rude nickname and wore it proudly. In English, they became the Ragamuffins.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="sm">Like a team turning a taunt into its own chant.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Source: Encyclopedia.com</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="l2iRm0VQRY" padding="0" colspan="29"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/8jBTD3SaPwf-j6PxWIgD9.png" saved-media-id="39lf2aqbrp0rimt" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper museum display of a weathered fringed leather riding jacket and folded cloth on warm cream paper, the rough edges treated as a proud team emblem, postcard red ribbon, river blue backing card and sun yellow pin, no person, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="s1ruglqmad"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="yadvW6AtpJ" vertical-align="center" colspan="28"><p role="eyebrow">The revolt begins</p><h2>20 September 1835: the day it began</h2><display size="md" font-size="38pt">Porto Alegre</display><p>Bento Gonçalves led rebel horsemen into the city and took it.</p><p>The empire won it back nine months later and held the coast. The Ragamuffins made the wide inland grasslands their home ground.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Source: Ragamuffin War overview</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="oxi8vynzUO" padding="0" colspan="32"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/NGGxmlB7O7LdzUApYfdOX.png" saved-media-id="n2t0uj9nceh9cif" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper landscape of peaceful horse riders approaching the distant rooftops of Porto Alegre across broad southern Brazilian grasslands at dawn, restrained documentary mood, historically grounded general clothing, postcard red route mark, river blue sky and sun yellow horizon, no combat, no weapons, no text" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="WSi5fO6I2O"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="zm80xNmZm3" vertical-align="center" colspan="23"><h2>They invented their own country</h2><p>After winning at Seival, the rebels declared the <b>Riograndense Republic</b> on 11 September 1836.</p><p>A republic is a country without an emperor. Bento Gonçalves became its first president.</p><blockquote><p><i>Liberty, Equality, Humanity</i></p></blockquote><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Source: Ragamuffin War overview</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="KFQ5dI-L8y" vertical-align="center" colspan="37"><freeform-block w="500" h="330"><box type="content" w="500" h="330" sizing="fixed"><custom-code>
            <style>
              .republic-map { width: 500px; height: 330px; font-family: var(--body-font); }
              .republic-map .paper { fill: var(--surface-color); stroke: var(--palette-5); stroke-width: 3; }
              .republic-map .fold { stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--palette-5) 60%, transparent); stroke-width: 2; stroke-dasharray: 8 7; }
              .republic-map .province { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--palette-2) 22%, white); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 4; stroke-linejoin: round; }
              .republic-map .republic { fill: var(--accent-color); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 4; stroke-linejoin: round; }
              .republic-map .flag { fill: var(--palette-3); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 3; }
            </style>
            <svg class="republic-map" width="500" height="330" viewBox="0 0 500 330" role="img" aria-label="Folded schematic map showing the Riograndense Republic inside southern Brazil">
              <path class="paper" d="M24 26 L170 14 L325 30 L478 18 L470 306 L322 316 L171 300 L30 314 Z"></path>
              <line class="fold" x1="170" y1="14" x2="171" y2="300"></line>
              <line class="fold" x1="325" y1="30" x2="322" y2="316"></line>
              <path class="province" d="M105 96 L216 69 L338 87 L410 153 L374 236 L262 270 L138 232 L79 163 Z"></path>
              <path class="republic" d="M121 119 L218 88 L318 101 L379 158 L349 214 L254 247 L157 216 L98 160 Z"></path>
              <line x1="286" y1="90" x2="286" y2="47" stroke="var(--body-color)" stroke-width="4"></line>
              <path class="flag" d="M288 48 L360 63 L288 83 Z"></path>
            </svg>
          </custom-code></box><box type="content" x="133" y="132" w="235" h="76" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 12pt 16pt; border-radius: 12pt;"><h3 align="center">Riograndense Republic</h3><p font-size="sm" align="center">Declared in 1836</p></box><box type="content" x="291" y="35" w="150" h="49" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-3" style="padding: 8pt 10pt; border-radius: 999pt;"><p align="center"><b>New flag marker</b></p></box></freeform-block></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="aJRpFY5-co"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="-tr7biidgO"><h2>Ten years, six moments</h2><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="20"><smart-layout-item><h4>1835</h4><p>Rebels take Porto Alegre.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>1836</h4><p>The Riograndense Republic is declared.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>1837</h4><p>Bento Gonçalves escapes prison and returns.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>1839</h4><p>Boats cross land; Laguna falls; Juliana is born.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>1842</h4><p>The Baron of Caxias takes command.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>1845</h4><p>Peace at Ponche Verde.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Source: Ragamuffin War overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-JESZEZ0xx" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="OIZgRMHlZi"><h2>Meet the Ragamuffins</h2><grid spacing="small" image-aspect="square" image-shape="circle"><grid-item id="tDP4apti3L" colspan="12"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/EiXQK3CAjl75hUmszeDJ9.png" saved-media-id="zeepifb9o7xduj8" source="image.ai-generated" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper portrait of Brazilian cattle rancher Bento Gonçalves, calm middle-aged expression, historically grounded non-specific 1830s clothing, warm cream paper with postcard red and river blue accents, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Bento Gonçalves</h4><p font-size="sm">Rancher, president and prison escaper.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UK_4aqOvgp" colspan="12"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/iitmEriFUbjzrkwI7CoA9.png" saved-media-id="n4h753bysfrffsk" source="image.ai-generated" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper portrait of Italian sailor Giuseppe Garibaldi during the 1830s, calm expression, simple historically grounded sailor clothing, warm cream paper with river blue and sun yellow accents, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Giuseppe Garibaldi</h4><p font-size="sm">Sailor who ran the rebel navy.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OPTz-mfCPS" colspan="12"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/2Oz6PmmMcBephzcE71AmR.png" saved-media-id="fi7y6jw68sb9035" source="image.ai-generated" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper portrait of Brazilian rider and sailor Anita Garibaldi, dignified calm expression, historically grounded non-specific 1830s clothing, warm cream paper with postcard red and sun yellow accents, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Anita Garibaldi</h4><p font-size="sm">Brazilian rider and sailor.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="MdijNW92pu" colspan="12"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/ek5UxoHn5I9jMPhDVvW7x.png" saved-media-id="atj2n23jo4avn7u" source="image.ai-generated" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper portrait of Brazilian general Antônio de Sousa Neto, restrained friendly expression, historically grounded non-specific 1830s clothing, warm cream paper with river blue accents, no uniform details, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Antônio de Sousa Neto</h4><p font-size="sm">Announced the new republic.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XnxenJpmO4" colspan="12"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/-thme_RZG2kz7OBOWh4eT.png" saved-media-id="avtctwytupnl045" source="image.ai-generated" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper portrait of Brazilian commander David Canabarro, restrained friendly expression, historically grounded non-specific 1830s clothing, warm cream paper with postcard red and sun yellow accents, no uniform details, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>David Canabarro</h4><p font-size="sm">Led the march on Laguna.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Sources and biographies</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="h27v6pr2RI" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/X9To5xMe7bDsPNAxS5nO-.png" saved-media-id="tkfn5s5bpb3uxlp" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Wide layered cut-paper hero illustration of a full-sized sailing boat resting on an enormous wooden wheeled carriage, pulled across southern Brazilian grassland by a very long line of oxen with a few dignified handlers walking beside them, marsh and sand ahead, postcard red wheels, river blue sail shadows and sun yellow daylight, soft colored-pencil shading, no text, no weapons, no combat" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><freeform><box type="content" x="700" y="48" w="205" h="82" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 12pt 16pt; border-radius: 14pt;"><p role="eyebrow" align="center">1839</p><h3 align="center">Six days over land</h3></box><box type="content" x="44" y="346" w="872" h="158" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 18pt 24pt; border-radius: 16pt;"><h2>The time they put boats on wheels</h2><p>Imperial warships blocked the lagoon. Garibaldi lifted two boats onto giant wooden carts. Around 100 oxen pulled each boat about 100 km across fields, sand and marsh. At Tramandaí, the boats splashed back into water unnoticed.</p><p role="caption"><a href="http://www.pampalivre.info/revolucao_farroupilha_a_epopeia_dos_lanchoes_pelos_campos_gauchos.htm">Source: Pampa Livre</a></p></box></freeform></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Rd_M5FeRQm"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="G_ouHJg2Fx" background-color="palette-2" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="lg">4</display><h3>months</h3><p>The short life of the Juliana Republic.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="rmK32cKGq2" vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><h2>A second republic, for four months</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical"><grid-item id="ZXN0eTxvLy" padding="12pt 0"><h4>22 July 1839</h4><p>The boat trick worked. The Ragamuffins captured Laguna.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="osqF1CwTDu" padding="12pt 0"><h4>A new declaration</h4><p>They announced the Juliana Republic in the neighbouring province.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1KwWRIhMH8" padding="12pt 0"><h4>The port is retaken</h4><p>About four months later, the empire returned. One rebel boat had already sunk in a storm; Garibaldi swam out alive.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Source: Ragamuffin War overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="xMb7RQGJZY"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="8FdpQsIDHr" padding="0" colspan="23"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/IMv7mncbQjYkXEXhw89OK.png" saved-media-id="c7uv7i3x8ao130d" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Dignified layered cut-paper group portrait of Black Lancers, freed and formerly enslaved men standing together in calm non-heroic poses, varied ages and skin tones, historically grounded but non-specific 1830s southern Brazilian clothing, warm cream paper, muted postcard red and river blue accents, no text, no weapons, no combat" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="UnQqw9MKFn" vertical-align="center" colspan="37"><h2>A promise that was broken</h2><grid direction="vertical" spacing="medium"><grid-item id="xlSxSCQAYE" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line"><p role="eyebrow">The promise</p><h3>The Black Lancers</h3><p>From 1836, the rebels formed units of freed and formerly enslaved men. Some were promised freedom for fighting.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="zdXcqLL-F_" background-color="accent"><p role="eyebrow">What happened</p><h3>The promise was not kept</h3><p>The republic's 1843 constitution kept slavery. Most rebel leaders enslaved people themselves, and many Black Lancers never received the freedom they were promised.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Source: Ragamuffin War overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="BtmEB2ZMB2" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="wC6RhxqrFN"><p role="eyebrow">Treaty of Ponche Verde · 1 March 1845</p><h2>How it ended: a deal, not a battle</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" spacing="small" padding-top="34pt"><grid-item id="oiaAvgAMd_" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/xo4JFjiDSlQp1cplsQVT.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="official pardon document" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black seal or crest silhouette on a white background, embodying the concept of authenticity and formality.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Pardons</h4><p>Everyone was pardoned.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FzWLfABts3" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/6FXAuU2pLPf3ursjSwNq7P.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="soldiers joining one group" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black helmet with a distinctive chin strap, set against a clean white background, symbolizing a soldier's protective gear and serving as a concise icon for the military or defense concept.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>One army</h4><p>Rebel soldiers joined the imperial army.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="LxiLOZfqoe" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/45fY7DLQboNL6ktut2xa.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="governor ballot and paid bill" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black silhouette of a governor's emblem or crest, often symbolizing leadership and authority, positioned centrally on a clean white background, conveying a sense of governance and administration.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Local choices</h4><p>The south picked its next governor. The empire paid the republic's debts.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="c7fzyHIDtm" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/bI1NKwwyoF20IGvcZrab.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="salted beef coin tax" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A stylized black cow's head with minimalist features, set against a clean white background, symbolizing beef.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>25% tax</h4><p>Imported charque finally received the tax the ranchers wanted.</p></grid-item></grid><aside><p>They gave up their republic, but won much of the argument that had started the revolt.</p></aside><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Source: Treaty summary</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="yHSNcIGTp1"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="xXDA2UlJiW" background-color="palette-3" vertical-align="center" colspan="21"><display size="xl">10</display><h3>years</h3><p>1835 to 1845. Brazil's biggest and longest regional revolt.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="rmV2-t14ah" vertical-align="center" colspan="39"><h2>Why people still talk about it</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" spacing="medium"><grid-item id="vpmA9rwwr7"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/p2KcT3AQIMR4CVEFqTvT.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="calendar September twentieth" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Seven small squares in a single row, symbolizing the seven days of a week, conveying the concept of a calendar week.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>20 September</h4><p>Rio Grande do Sul still celebrates the date every year.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="b1FDdpEe4C"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/mFiXglkNuAgHbRpa2lQ4.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="sailing ship route to Italy" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A stylized black silhouette of a ship with a distinctive curved structure at the back and a flat front, symbolizing a cruise-ship, likely used to represent vacation, travel, or leisure activities at sea.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Garibaldi's next chapter</h4><p>He sailed home and later helped unite Italy.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Y5wE05I4l_"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/vDfPhjW1ONQwpEVCjc24.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="proud cloth team badge" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A piece of cloth folded into a rectangular shape with a straight line at the top and a curved bottom, signifying the concept of fabric or textile.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>A nickname transformed</h4><p>“Farroupilha” changed from an insult into a badge of pride.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Source: Encyclopedia.com</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="3oKjJwjksd" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="PShNowkHRC"><p role="eyebrow">No peeking at the next slide</p><h2>Quiz time!</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" spacing="small" padding-top="42pt"><grid-item id="Ti1mmtv4fB" cell-style="subtle" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/bI1NKwwyoF20IGvcZrab.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="salted dried beef food" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A stylized black cow's head with minimalist features, set against a clean white background, symbolizing beef.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>What food started the whole argument?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="5PKpagaQmB" cell-style="subtle" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/9eg9RNQebKpKhCBhFg5bqe.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="frayed cloth rag" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A crude mop head with a long handle, conveying the concept of cleaning or a tool for scrubbing.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>What does <i>farrapo</i> mean?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="G8rkossuI7" cell-style="subtle" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/CdsdhEgYhJ80rcAjfc5A.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="young emperor crown" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Since there is no visual provided, I will assume a common symbol for \&quot;young\&quot;. \n\nA minimalist black baby or toddler icon in a white background, signifying youth, innocence, and new beginnings associated with the concept of being young.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>How old was Pedro II when the war began?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="uMc_mW7HRY" cell-style="subtle" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/7X3JnWz1eCevkJQl5W6p.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="sailing boat wooden cart oxen" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A triangular shape with a long curved base and two pointed corners at the top, symbolizing the concept of sail.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>How did Garibaldi pass the warships?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="wJ7yJwPJRT" cell-style="subtle" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/p2KcT3AQIMR4CVEFqTvT.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="calendar decade pages" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Seven small squares in a single row, symbolizing the seven days of a week, conveying the concept of a calendar week.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>How many years did the war last?</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="hPP5yUHevr" vertical-align="center" background-color="accent"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="dVYJKKmvGm"><h1>Answers</h1><grid divider="sm palette-3" marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" style="--marker-inline-size: 36pt; --marker-gap: 16pt;"><grid-item id="K8TT9wFyzQ" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Charque</h4><p>Salted dried beef.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="DktJZlwgb-" padding="10pt 0"><h4>“Rag”</h4><p>A nickname the rebels turned into a badge of honour.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="eHMzX4ZaAP" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Nine years old</h4><p>Grown-up regents ruled for Pedro II.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cGHwZTIqce" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Boats on carts</h4><p>Garibaldi rolled them overland with oxen.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hL3cmH3jm6" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Ten years</h4><p>From 1835 to 1845.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>